-- The Install step the sizing chain does not have.
--
-- The three manufacturer PDFs in pdf/ are already cited by INVERTER_PRESETS
-- and PANEL_PRESETS, and a visitor who picked that stack still has to be the
-- one who speaks both manuals. Factory default on the SPH is GEL. That is
-- differentiator #1 inverted, and it is a protection-register problem: a
-- "set Program 09 to 56.8 V" card is the Saloomey chart, not the Winter book.
--
-- Keep in sync with supabase/seed.sql (CI enforces this).

insert into public.roadmap_items
  (phase, category, title, description, status, dev_percent_complete, is_public, display_order)
values
  (1, 'calculators', 'System designer: commissioning map for chosen equipment',
   'The Install step the sizing chain does not have. Step 7 currently reads disagreements between calculators; it never tells someone with a chosen SPH10048P and SG48100P which LCD item to change, so they leave the factory GEL profile on a lithium pack. That is differentiator #1 inverted: the manuals are in pdf/ and already cited by INVERTER_PRESETS and PANEL_PRESETS, and the user still has to be the one who speaks both. NOT a cheat sheet and not a new calculator. A mapping, gated on admitted equipment IDs, rendered on /calculators/system through ProtectionOutput. Each row is a ProtectionView: the inverter menu item, the set of options that pass, the arithmetic, and both manuals cited. Never a single "set Program 09 to 56.8 V." "Recommended" is rejected by assertProtectionView, same as the rest of the protection register. WHY THIS IS PROTECTION, NOT CAPACITY. Wrong charge voltage, wrong battery type, equalize left on, or a generator charge current above what the machine can supply, destroy equipment or stall a generator. The existing cutoff-voltage output already classified the stop-using-the-battery half; this item is the rest of that menu, equipment-specific. Work mode (UTI/SBU/SOL/SUB) is a use-case choice and stays out of the protection register -- the map asks which job the system has, it does not pick one. THE FAILURE THIS EXISTS TO PREVENT is picking a side of a datasheet conflict and putting the site''s authority behind it. Same brand, same three PDFs: the SG48100P sheet says charge at 54.5 V and stay in 20-95% SOC; the SPH L16 preset charges at 56.8 V; the inverter ships as GEL. The map must surface that disagreement the way system-design.ts surfaces the odd-panel-count mismatch, not resolve it. Lithium stop-using-the-battery is percent remaining after BMS comms (items 32/33 SGP, then 59/60/61), matching cutoffProtectionView. If comms are not confirmed, the option is "establish comms", not a voltage. GENERATOR IS AN INPUT, NOT A PV SETTING. The panel datasheet is already consumed by the array step (Voc vs 500 V, MPPT 125-425 V). Generator lives on AC-in plus the dry-contact auto-start in SPH manual 6.5, and needs the generator''s kW and whether it has ATS. Charge current is min(battery max x parallel count, inverter item 07/28, generator leftover after loads, cable ampacity). Missing any of those four, do not emit amps -- show the missing question. Item 03 UPS vs APL is generator-quality, also unanswered by these PDFs. V1 SCOPE is one admitted pairing: SPH8048P or SPH10048P + SG48100P, when those preset IDs are the ones chosen. Typed-in-by-hand specs, or an EG4 inverter against a Sun Gold battery, get the generic inverter-settings guide, not a map -- menu IDs are firmware-and-model-specific and a wrong ID is worse than none. The SG550WM does not appear on the map; its job is the array step. DATA SHAPE. battery_models cannot carry this: it has dod_rated and chemistry, not charge voltage, series count (16S), BMS protocol, or max charge current. Admit a BATTERY_PRESETS row (sibling of INVERTER_PRESETS) from the manufacturer''s own manual, with commissioning-review.ts catching transcription errors (voltage order 15<12<04<14<35<37<05<09, L16 is 16S not 15S, equalize off for LFP, GEL-default trap present). Every menu mapping cites manual + page. Tests lock the SPH L16 and SG48100P numbers to those pages so a later cleanup cannot silently pick 56.8. TRACK 1 IS NOT TRACK 2. The neighbor''s actual settings belong in neighbor-build/, dated to a firmware version. The public map generates the same derivation for anyone who selected this pairing. Do not paste the neighbor''s numbers into the product. Depends on the spec library admission gate and the protection-register chrome; it does not absorb either. The licensed-electrician sign-off, clickwrap, and professional-review items stay independent gates -- a bigger disclaimer is not a substitute, and showing the derivation of a WRONG number documents the error. Phase 1 rather than phase 0 because the product currently omits this output rather than emitting a wrong one. First phase-1 item to pick up after the spec library can admit a battery programming row.',
   'planned', 0, true, 101);
